## Rules

1. **Phase**: Look at the button text.
   - "叫地主"/"抢地主"/"不叫"/"不加倍" → bidding
   - "出牌"/"不出"/"提示" → playing

2. **Buttons** — EVERY visible button on screen:
   - text: exact Chinese text on the button
   - active: true if the button looks ENABLED (bright/vivid color), false if DISABLED (dim/grey/washed out)
     **This is the most critical field.** "提示" button:
     - active=true → AI hints available, click it
     - active=false → no hints, button is greyed out
   - x, y: pixel center of the button. Use the [0-1000] grid lines on the image as reference —
     align your coordinates to the nearest visible grid intersection.

3. **Hand cards**: One entry per card, LEFT to RIGHT. Only x, y needed.

4. **Coordinate accuracy**: Look at the white grid lines and numbers on the screenshot.
   Align your x,y values to the nearest grid line crossing. This ensures accurate positioning.

5. Output ONLY the JSON. No markdown, no explanation, no backticks.
